# Neural-network attack and defense evaluation

Model: 64-64-10 MLP on 8x8 handwritten digits (900 train / 450 test / 447 attacker pool).

- Fingerprint: `cfbea681599d6984`

## 1. Evasion: adversarial examples (ATLAS AML.T0015, AML.T0043)

Test accuracy when every pixel may change by at most ε (0..1 scale; 0.10 ≈ 1.6 of 16 gray levels).

| Model | Clean | FGSM ε=0.05 | FGSM ε=0.1 | FGSM ε=0.15 | PGD ε=0.05 | PGD ε=0.1 | PGD ε=0.15 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Undefended | 96.4% | 83.3% | 51.3% | 12.7% | 83.3% | 48.0% | 9.6% |
| Adversarially trained (ε=0.15) | 96.2% | 90.7% | 78.2% | 60.7% | 90.7% | 76.9% | 54.9% |

## 2. Poisoning: backdoor trigger (ATLAS AML.T0020, AML.T0018)

45 of 945 training images carry a 3-pixel corner trigger and the label 7. Backdoor success = share of non-7 test digits read as 7 once the trigger is added.

| Model | Clean accuracy | Backdoor success |
|---|---|---|
| Trained on clean data | 96.4% | 0.0% |
| Trained on poisoned data | 97.1% | 99.3% |
| Retrained after activation clustering | 95.1% | 5.2% |

Activation clustering removed **42 of 45** poisoned rows and **2** clean rows.

| Label | Smaller cluster | Model trained without it reads it as another digit (mean confidence) | Removed |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | 33 | 5% | no |
| 1 | 39 | 66% | no |
| 2 | 42 | 41% | no |
| 3 | 45 | 19% | no |
| 4 | 20 | 35% | no |
| 5 | 41 | 28% | no |
| 6 | 33 | 22% | no |
| 7 | 44 | 91% | **yes** |
| 8 | 42 | 57% | no |
| 9 | 16 | 54% | no |

Operating range: the same defense at other poison rates.

| Poisoned rows | Poison removed | Clean removed | Backdoor success after |
|---|---|---|---|
| 20 | 19 | 2 | 1.3% |
| 45 | 42 | 2 | 5.2% |
| 90 | 0 | 0 | 99.5% |

## 3. Extraction: cloning through the API (ATLAS AML.T0024.002)

Victim clean accuracy 96.4%. Transferred FGSM: ε=0.10 examples crafted on the clone only, then sent to the victim.

| API returns | Query budget | Queries answered | Clone agrees with victim | Victim accuracy on transferred attack |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| probs | none | 900 | 97.8% | 68.7% |
| label | none | 900 | 96.0% | 71.3% |
| label | 50 | 50 | 80.2% | 82.4% |

## 4. Membership inference (ATLAS AML.T0024.000)

Model trained on 100 images. Advantage = best (true-positive rate − false-positive rate) at telling those images from unseen ones; 0 is a coin flip.

| Training | API returns | Test accuracy | Attack advantage |
|---|---|---|---|
| overfit (300 epochs, no L2) | probs | 90.4% | 0.37 |
| overfit (300 epochs, no L2) | label | 90.4% | 0.09 |
| regularized (L2 0.02) | probs | 90.4% | 0.28 |
| regularized (L2 0.02) | label | 90.4% | 0.08 |

## 5. Supply chain: malicious model file (ATLAS AML.T0010.003, AML.T0011)

| Load | Attacker code ran | Result |
|---|---|---|
| `pickle.load` of the malicious file | **YES** | model still works (96.4%), so nobody notices |
| `safe_load` of the malicious file | no | refused: hash 766ab9fd6e8d... does not match the pinned bf1a37e8c35d... |
| `safe_load` of the genuine file | no | loads, accuracy 96.4% |
| `safe_load` of tampered weights (.npz) | no | refused: hash dce9bad36f7b... does not match the pinned bf1a37e8c35d... |

report written to reports/nn_eval.md
